New Hotline Features:
- Banner support (integrate into Toolbar?)

System Notifications:
- Support system notifications

Chat:
- Better formatting (use <nick> instead of nick:)
- Draggable separator between names and text, just like HexChat has
- Better line/word wrap handling
- Make input box shorter in height by default. It should expand to multi line input as necessary
- Highlight name on mention, support additional highlight words in config

General:
- Help feature within GtkHx. It should at least explain available keyboard shortcuts.

Docs:
- Rewrite README to explain this project better
- Write a section about migrating from 0.9.4 to modern versions

i18n:
- Translate to other languages

Security:
- Default to encryption on? Can we tell if a server supports encryption? If not, we can try connecting with encryption first, and then fallback to no encryption
- Look into what newer Hotline clients/servers support (ties into mhxd epic)

Pulling in any new developments from over the years:
- Look into rebasing hx-specific code (especially anything protocol related) from mhxd
- Also look into any fixes from ghx in mhxd -- it does have some stuff taken from GtkHx like news15.c

File Previews:
- Look into using some sort of library that lets us view different file types with some embedded viewer
  e.g. There's an RTF file on some server and it would be nice to preview the rendered version of it

Bookmarks
- Better bookmark management, allowing user to add/edit/delete bookmarks

Tracker
- Ship with some more built in trackers configured

Code Modernization:
- Better modules with more code reuse
- Define string / resource consts instead of repeating them (or having them littered throughout the code)
- Separation of concerns -- separate UI code from non-UI code
- Follow MVC architecture

Code Cleanup:
- Remove #define/#ifdef/#ifndef for things like USE_IPV6 and other things we should just consider a given these days

Features:
- Custom color palette
- Log chat history / server, and be able to bring that chat history back up when connecting to a server


Old:
-Full file support (not sure what this means)
-Reimplement SOCKS support (see mhxd source)
